From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DE25-Nano Port <de25-nano@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover Menu before DE25 MMIO

When a core leaves the lightweight HPS bridge inaccessible, the first Main
register access raises SIGBUS. A systemd restart has no core arguments, so use
that unambiguous condition to reload the known-good Menu through the privileged
FPGA-region helper before mapping or touching the bridge. Core handoff restarts
carry the selected RBF in argv and therefore retain the newly loaded core.
---
 main.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main.cpp b/main.cpp
index 97a3c2b..e508176 100644
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,17 @@ const char *version = "$VER:" VDATE;
 
 int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 {
+#ifdef MISTER_DE25
+	// A service start or crash restart has no selected-core argument. Restore
+	// Menu before the first MMIO access so an inaccessible bridge cannot trap
+	// Main in a SIGBUS restart loop.
+	if (argc == 1 && system("/usr/libexec/mister-de25-load /media/fat/menu.rbf"))
+	{
+		fprintf(stderr, "Unable to recover DE25 Menu fabric image\n");
+		return 1;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	// Always pin main worker process to core #1 as core #0 is the
 	// hardware interrupt handler in Linux.  This reduces idle latency
 	// in the main loop by about 6-7x.
